{
  "summary": "Introduces a minimal `linux-base-gcc` toolchain variant in Guix for non-GUI static Linux builds, disabling unused `libstdc++` features (`--disable-wchar_t`, `--enable-clocale=generic`, and `--with-libstdcxx-zoneinfo=no`). It also disables the experimental `libstdc++fs` library across Linux GCC builds and adds a patch in `depends` so Boost Test compiles without `std::wcrtomb`.",
  "problem": "Guix non-GUI Linux release binaries link unused `libstdc++` components such as wide-character handling, timezone info, and the experimental filesystem TS library, unnecessarily inflating binary sizes.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author measurements demonstrate ~0.48 MB size reductions across non-GUI binaries (bitcoind drops from 17.75 MB to 17.27 MB, bitcoin-cli from 8.20 MB to 7.72 MB)."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Dropped commits associated with PR #36531 (including changes to Guix module loading via `--load-path`), removing the dependency on that PR.",
  "card": "Introduces a minimal linux-base-gcc toolchain variant for non-GUI Linux static Guix builds, disabling unused libstdc++ features including wide-character support, zoneinfo, and the filesystem TS library. It also patches Boost Test in depends to invoke wcrtomb without std namespace qualification to maintain compatibility without wchar_t support. This reduces release binary sizes for tools like bitcoind and bitcoin-cli by roughly 0.5 MB.",
